    ],
    "note": "In the clothes senses, **dress** takes a person as its object (*dress the baby*) or none (*she dressed quickly*). **Put on** is the action of getting clothes onto your body (*put on your shoes*). **Wear** is having clothes on your body (*she's wearing a red coat*)."
  },
  "usage_note": "In everyday speech, **get dressed** is more usual than **dress** for putting on your own clothes.",
  "learner_errors": [
